Each front fender now uses one fitted radial surface across its top and side.
The fit retains all 1,379 measured stations per side within 7.75 mm and supplies
a continuous tangent field. Simplification explicitly retains the 1,044 source
vertices shared by each tier's fender cut and its remaining neighbour. A native
vertex-group probe and the conversion's exact-coordinate assertion verify this
constraint. The measured side skins preserve the transverse factory profile;
local handle fairing removes the recessed-looking highlight beneath the drawn
outline. Door joins have at most 2.94 degrees of normal change at the checked
crossings. These are sampled geometry/shading measurements, not an AAA claim.

Each window has a single exterior skin and its own measured smooth curvature.
The opaque backing is inset clear of the panes. Native rays reproduce the old
backing protruding through the rear glass and verify the correction. The old
rear applique, lens pockets and raised lettering are removed from the area
occupied by the authored smoked panel and tail lamps; its outer return now
covers the source opening. The white-body/red-accent view checks the defects
that were difficult to see in default dark trim.

